(2) THE PARITY EXTENSION: the LRC seven is n/2, an INTEGER only for even n
    hhat(m) = sin(2*pi*m/n)/(pi*m) vanishes iff n | 2m, i.e. m = 0 mod n/gcd(2,n)
      n even -> zeros every n/2 steps (DENSE)
      n odd  -> zeros every n steps   (half as dense)
    n= 12: hhat zeros every   6 steps;  n/2 = 6 (INTEGER)   arity ceiling k < n/2 is exact
    n= 13: hhat zeros every  13 steps;  n/2 = 6.5 (not an integer)   arity ceiling k < n/2 never degenerates exactly
    n= 14: hhat zeros every   7 steps;  n/2 = 7 (INTEGER)   arity ceiling k < n/2 is exact
    n= 15: hhat zeros every  15 steps;  n/2 = 7.5 (not an integer)   arity ceiling k < n/2 never degenerates exactly
    n= 16: hhat zeros every   8 steps;  n/2 = 8 (INTEGER)   arity ceiling k < n/2 is exact
    n= 17: hhat zeros every  17 steps;  n/2 = 8.5 (not an integer)   arity ceiling k < n/2 never degenerates exactly

(3) THE TENT/INDEPENDENCE COINCIDENCE ACROSS n  (THM-1195 was n=14)
    tent threshold = lam/2 = 1/(2n); independence E[min] = (1/2)/(n_speeds+1)
    with n_speeds = n-1 these agree iff 1/(2n) = 1/(2n) -- ALWAYS.
    n= 10: tent 1/20  independence 1/20   EQUAL
    n= 12: tent 1/24  independence 1/24   EQUAL
    n= 13: tent 1/26  independence 1/26   EQUAL
    n= 14: tent 1/28  independence 1/28   EQUAL
    n= 20: tent 1/40  independence 1/40   EQUAL
    => the coincidence THM-1195 found at n=14 is NOT special to 14: it holds
       for every n, and is the statement that LRC's floor sits exactly where
       the geometric and probabilistic estimates cross.
